+/**
+ * sde_get_ddrtype - read the DDR device type described by the DT memory
+ *	nodes (replacement for the donor-only of_fdt_get_ddrtype())
+ *
+ * The donor kernel decoded the DDR type inside drivers/of/fdt.c. That
+ * helper is not part of the paired 6.18 kernel, so the display driver reads
+ * the same information from the real DT memory nodes: every node of type
+ * "memory" may carry the bootloader-provided "ddr_device_type" property.
+ * Missing property, missing memory node or conflicting values are reported
+ * as a negative errno; callers must fall back to a documented default
+ * instead of assuming a DDR generation.
